  "worked_solution": "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x-y)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{11\\pi }{12}) & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{7\\pi }{6}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{7\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{7\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
